  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef calculus_linreg_gradient(X: list, y: list, w: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Gradient of Multivariate Linear Regression Loss** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef calculus_linreg_gradient(X: list, y: list, w: list) -> dict:\n    Xa, ya, wa = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y, dtype=np.float64), np.array(w, dtype=np.float64)\n    diff = np.dot(Xa, wa) - ya\n    return {'mse_loss': round(float(np.mean(diff**2)), 6), 'gradient': np.round((2.0 / len(Xa)) * np.dot(Xa.T, diff), 6).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
